_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/me-steven/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/me-steven/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/me-steven/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/me-steven/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/me-steven/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/me-steven/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T03:49:14Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T04:05:44Z","body":"Seems like if your 2D Node doesn't have it's scale set to 1.0 on X and Y it'll fail to transform the 3D Node properly.\n\nIt mostly changes the scale of X and Y to the same values as the 2D node but sets Z to 0. Sometimes it'll set every axis to 0.\n\nDoesn't matter if you're scale is larger or smaller than 1.0, if it's not 1 on both X and Y it'll fail.\n\nSeems to be agnostic of the specific nodes, just if it goes from 2D to 3D.\n\nAlso tried with a Control node -> 3D and it also failed.\n\n2D -> Control and Control -> 2D work fine.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314492293/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]